    <text>
        <body>
            <div xml:id="d420">

                <pb facs="0422" n="410" sameAs="frus:frus1944v05/pg410"/>

                <note rend="inline" type="source">891.51A/1165: Telegram</note>
                <head>
                    <hi rendition="#italic">The Chargé in Iran</hi> (<hi
                            rendition="#italic">Ford</hi>) <hi rendition="#italic">to the
                            Secretary of State
                    </hi>
                </head>
                <opener>
                    <dateline rendition="#float-right">
                        <placeName>
                            <hi rendition="#small-caps">Tehran</hi></placeName>, <date
                            calendar="gregorian" when="1944-06-13T12:00:00+03:25">June 13,
                            1944—noon</date>.<lb/>[Received June 13—10:12 a.m.]</dateline>
                </opener>
                <p>422. I wish to warn Department that Ebtehaj has turned violently against
                    Millspaugh and open warfare has broken out between the two men. Speaking before
                    Tehran Chamber of Commerce few days ago, Ebtehaj said: “Five days after I reach
                    Washington, Millspaugh will be removed.”<anchor n="10" xml:id="d420-f1"/>
                </p>
                <p>My letter June 9 to George Allen<anchor n="11" xml:id="d420-f2"/> gives details
                    of Ebtehaj’s attitude.</p>
                <closer>
                    <signed>
                        <hi rendition="#small-caps">Ford</hi>
                    </signed>
                </closer>
            </div>
        </body>
    </text>
    <standOff>
        <listAnnotation>
            <note corresp="#d420-f1" n="10" xml:id="d420-f1-content">
                <p>Abol Hassan Ebtehaj had been appointed Chairman of the Iranian delegation to the
                    United Nations Monetary and Financial Conference to be held at Bretton Woods,
                    New Hampshire, July 1–July 22, 1944; for correspondence regarding this
                    Conference, see <ref target="frus1944v02">vol. <hi rendition="#small-caps"
                            >ii</hi>
                    </ref>.</p>
            </note>
            <note corresp="#d420-f2" n="11" xml:id="d420-f2-content">
                <p>Chief of the Division of Middle Eastern Affairs.</p>
            </note>
        </listAnnotation>
    </standOff>
